From 85b458b83d8ab3b4861f5ee636a2491dec127f3b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 20:03:57 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] docs(site): Zola documentation site, deployed to GitHub
 Pages at each release tag

A Zola project at site/ with our own templates (no third-party theme):
a user guide (install, first run, setups, operations, posting, reading a
refusal) and a short developer section (crate map, commands and undo,
test gates, releases), written from the README, AGENTS.md and the code.
The front page shows the version the site was built from and says the
browser build is coming (#31).

release.yml gains a `site` job (pinned Zola v0.23.6, checksum-verified,
builds the tagged tree with the repo's Pages URL as base) and a `pages`
job (actions/deploy-pages, pages: write + id-token: write scoped to it)
that deploys only on a tag once the release page is published. No new
trigger. site/public/ and site/version.toml are gitignored.

Refs #688

